clear() se saare elements delete ho jate hain.
Time Complexity of HashSet Operations
Operation	Average Case	Worst Case (Collision)
Insertion (add)	O(1)	O(n)
Deletion (remove)	O(1)	O(n)
Searching (contains)	O(1)	O(n)
When to Use HashSet?
✅ Jab aapko unique elements store karne ho.
✅ Jab aapko fast search, insert aur delete operations chahiye.
✅ Jab ordering important nahi ho.

When NOT to Use HashSet?
❌ Jab insertion order maintain karni ho, use LinkedHashSet.
❌ Jab sorted elements chahiye, use TreeSet.

Conclusion
HashSet ek powerful data structure hai jo unique values store karta hai.
HashMap internally use karta hai, isliye fast operations provide karta hai.
Duplicates allow nahi karta aur ordering maintain nahi karta.
Average case me O(1) complexity hoti hai for most operations.
